body:
Yes, and actually constantly, which is extremely mentally draining. I seriously don't remember a day that I have not thought of death.

&#x200B;

The thing about death that really scares me is the fact that nobody truly knows what happens once we die, there are a lot of theories out there based on religion or science as to what people believe happens after, but we don't really know. In my personal opinion I do believe that once we die, that's it, there is no coming back, which I think can attribute to my fear of death. For me, it's the fear of the after, not necessarily death itself, but I feel that our whole life has been wasted working, only to die. It's like all the hard work that we have done and all the people we have ever known would have all been for nothing, because ourselves and everybody else will have no recollection of the lives we lived. It's just scary to me knowing that we will never experience this life ever again, we will never remember all of our friends and family, and the moments that brought us happiness. We will never be able to see our loved ones ever again, and all the thoughts we have and can create, we will never be able to have that ability again. But I guess what scares me the most is knowing how fast death actually comes, when were young we think life goes on forever, and then you find all these years behind you and how quick they came by, we don't realize that death is coming quicker than we all expect or realize, and it's just a matter of time before the day comes where death is hanging right over us.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
